findings.body:
The probe compares each session's recorded `tmux_target` with every pane id a default server lists. It does this for every row `listTaskSessions` returns, killed and merged ones included:

```ts
function listsWindow(panes: string, row: SessionRow): boolean {
  return panes.split('\n').some((line) => {
    const [pane, name] = line.split(' ');
    return pane === row.tmux_target || name === `pup-${row.id}`;
  });
}
```

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/a06b91187f4b114ac9c6362d7d2ef17cea31a109/src/core/task-rescope.service.ts#L119-L124 (called at [L177-L186](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/a06b91187f4b114ac9c6362d7d2ef17cea31a109/src/core/task-rescope.service.ts#L177-L186))

`tmux_target` holds a `%N` pane id (`new-session -P -F '#{pane_id}'`), and that id stays set after the window is gone:
- The gate's merge teardown calls `killTmux(session.id, session.tmux_target)` and leaves the column set (`merge-gate.service.ts:1579`).
- A plain `pup kill` leaves it set too (`session-lifecycle.service.ts:859`). Only the fix-round branch nulls it.

A new tmux server numbers its panes from `%0` again. The codebase already knows this: `fix-round.service.ts:906` says "the pane id the gate recorded can be another window's once tmux has restarted".

This hits the feature's main use case. A merged session is waiting on a CI fix round, and the gate's teardown closed the last window, so the default server exits. The probe then refuses because no server answers, and the ADR's advice is to start one. The new server's first pane can then carry the merged session's old id. Every `pup plan edit <task> --rescope` is refused with "Session X's window may still be open". `tmux ls` shows no `pup-X`, and nothing points the operator at the colliding pane, so the hand edit of `state.db` this ADR was written to replace is the only way out.

Possible fixes:
- Null `tmux_target` when the gate's teardown and `pup kill` take the window down, as the fix-round kill path already does.
- Or match by name only for rows in a terminal state (merged, killed).

Please add a test where a merged row's recorded pane id shows up under another session's name.
